Please find below the Lancashire Local Resilience Forum situation report for Storm Fenella response.

Report no.   | 5
Date/time    | 15 January 2026, 12:00
Status       | Active response
Coastal      | Overtopping at high tide on the Morecambe frontage. Next high tide 1015.
Responding   | Lancashire Constabulary, Network Rail, Lancaster City Council, Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service

Locations:
  * West End Community Centre: open as rest centre (run by Lancaster City Council)
  * A683 Lancaster to Kirkby Lonsdale: closed - flooding (run by LCC)
  * the WCML between Carlisle and Lancaster: services resumed
  * Carnforth primary: damaged by flood water (run by Electricity North West)

Next update to follow after the TCG.

